LOCATION:Kendall Square\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Times: 1pm\, 4:20pm\, 7:05pm\nFrom director and writer Marie Kr
 eutzer (Corsage\, Austria’s entry for the 95th Academy Awards)\, Gentle 
 Monster tells the story of concert pianist Lucy (Léa Seydoux)\, who has j
 ust relocated her family to a country house hoping to ease her husband Phi
 lip’s (Laurence Rupp) severe burnout. Before they have a chance to set u
 p their new home\, an early morning police visit tears their life apart. T
 rapped between the man she loves and the fear of what he may have done\, L
 ucy must face the situation alone as her world unravels. With a cast that 
 includes Jella Haase alongside the legendary\, Academy Award nominee Cathe
 rine Deneuve\, Gentle Monster asks what we do when someone we love turns o
 ut to be someone we never really knew.\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.c
